# UI and UX

Design the user job, journey, and information hierarchy before decoration. Do not ship a generic card grid, gradient wallpaper, or chatbot clone as the default.

Use a clear type hierarchy, consistent spacing, and intentional whitespace. Motion explains a change of state; it does not decorate.

Target WCAG 2.2 AA where practical: contrast, focus visibility, labels, errors tied to fields, and hit targets that work on touch.

AI surfaces show progress, uncertainty, citations or provenance when answers depend on sources, tool activity when tools run, and a recovery path after failure. Do not expose internal agent topology as the product UI.

Destructive actions require a specific confirmation and an obvious recovery path when recovery exists.
